IMPORT prelude

-- Lifelong Learning Endowment Fund Act 2001 (Singapore) -- what the income of the Fund may pay for and for whom (s 5), gifts and
-- capital (s 4(2)-(4)), expenses (s 7), the authorisation rule (s 10), the financial year (s 8), who may audit (s 11(1), (2)), the
-- offences (ss 12, 14), liability of directors, partners and officers (s 15), composition (s 16), and the Advisory Council's
-- removal, quorum and voting rules (Schedule paras 1(3), 3, 6).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LLEFA2001.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". Its legislative
-- history lists only Act 1 of 2001 (commenced 12 March 2001) and the 2002 Revised Edition; no amending Act is annotated. The SSO
-- metadata beside it reads "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0181 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has yet
-- asked a sharper question. The Act is short (17 sections and a Schedule) and almost all of it is about the Fund itself, so the
-- SCOPE is what a learner, a training provider, a donor, or someone questioned by the auditor actually meets. Not encoded: the
-- establishment of the Fund and its banking and investment (ss 3, 4(1)), the Council's establishment and chair (s 6), the
-- Minister's accounting and reporting duties (ss 9, 13), the auditor's access, report contents and reporting (s 11(3)-(6)),
-- regulation-making (s 17), and the rest of the Schedule (paras 1(1), (2), 2, 4, 5, 7). No regulations made under s 17 were
-- retrieved, so how anyone applies for money, and whether any offence is prescribed as compoundable, is unknown here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Lifelong Learning Endowment Fund Act 2001 -- the Fund`

§§ `5 -- what the income of the Fund may pay for`

-- s 5(1): the objects are "(a) the acquisition of skills and expertise by persons, and the development and upgrading of skills and
-- expertise of persons, to enhance their employability; and (b) the promotion of" the same.
-- s 5(2): the Minister "may, from time to time, authorise the income of the Fund to be paid out and expended for" (a) "financial
-- assistance or incentives to persons to acquire, develop or upgrade, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, skills and expertise to
-- enhance their employability"; (b) research or development "in or of learning methods and technology"; (c) promotion; (d)
-- financial assistance or incentives to persons to carry out "activities or programmes which are consistent with the objects";
-- (e) "the establishment, expansion or maintenance of facilities"; (f) any other consistent purpose "that are prescribed".
--
-- The Act says "persons" throughout. It sets no citizenship, residence or age condition, and every head says "whether in Singapore
-- or elsewhere". Whatever limits apply to a particular scheme are not in this Act. Learning that is not aimed at employability
-- (a hobby course) is outside (a) and fits only if prescribed under (f).
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `assistance to a person to upgrade skills for employability`
    `research into learning methods and technology`
    `promoting skills upgrading`
    `assistance to a person to run a programme consistent with the objects`
    `building or maintaining a training facility`
    `assistance for a leisure course unrelated to employability`
    `a general subsidy unrelated to skills`

DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `a citizen`
    `a permanent resident`
    `a foreigner`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `prescribed under s 5(2)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is one the income may be spent on` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `assistance for a leisure course unrelated to employability` THEN `prescribed under s 5(2)(f)`
    WHEN `a general subsidy unrelated to skills` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 5(2)(a): the person's status and where the learning happens play no part in whether the purpose is within the Act.
GIVEN `the status` IS A Status, `the learning is outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the purpose` IS A Purpose,
      `prescribed under s 5(2)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act permits assisting this person` IF
    `the purpose is one the income may be spent on` `the purpose` `prescribed under s 5(2)(f)`

§§ `4(3), 5(2) and 10 -- whether a payment may be made`

-- s 4(3): "The capital money of the Endowment Fund must not be used for any purpose other than for investment."
-- s 10: "A payment must not be made out of the Endowment Fund unless the payment is authorised by the Minister."
-- s 5(2): the Minister "may" authorise -- nothing in the Act gives anyone a right to be paid.
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `prescribed under s 5(2)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid from capital` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment may be made` IF
        (NOT `paid from capital`)
    AND `authorised by the Minister`
    AND `the purpose is one the income may be spent on` `the purpose` `prescribed under s 5(2)(f)`

§§ `4(2) -- gifts and bequests`

-- s 4(2): "Despite the terms of any gift or bequest, all gifts and bequests given or made for the purposes of the Endowment Fund must
-- be paid into the Fund as capital money." With s 4(3), such a gift may only be invested; only its income is ever spent, whatever
-- the donor directs.
GIVEN `given for the purposes of the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN, `the donor directs that it be spent at once` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gift becomes capital that may only be invested` IF
    `given for the purposes of the Fund`

§§ `4(4) and 7 -- what income is left to pay out`

-- s 4(4): "Where at any time there is a permanent diminution of the capital money of the Endowment Fund, the Minister must, before
-- paying out any income of the Fund, make good the diminution from the income of the Fund."
-- s 7: "All expenses incurred in connection with the administration of the Endowment Fund, including the cost of auditing the
-- accounts of the Fund, must be defrayed out of the income of the Fund."
-- Both come off income here and the result is floored at nil. The Act does not order the two against each other or say what
-- happens when income falls short; the floor is an inference.
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below nil` MEANS
    IF `amount` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `amount`

GIVEN `the year's income` IS A NUMBER, `permanent diminution not yet made good` IS A NUMBER, `administration and audit expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income available to pay out` MEANS
    `not below nil` (`the year's income` MINUS `permanent diminution not yet made good` MINUS `administration and audit expenses`)

§§ `8 -- the financial year`

-- s 8: "The financial year of the Endowment Fund begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
-- Given a calendar month (1-12) and year, the year in which that financial year began.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year began in` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` MINUS 1

§§ `11(1), (2) -- who may audit the Fund`

-- s 11(1): audited "by the Auditor-General or any other auditor that may be appointed annually by the Minister after consulting the
-- Auditor-General". (2): "A person is not qualified for appointment as an auditor under subsection (1) unless the person is a public
-- accountant within the meaning of the Companies Act 1967."
-- READING (an inference): (2) is read as applying to the other auditor the Minister appoints, not to the Auditor-General.
GIVEN `is the Auditor-General` IS A BOOLEAN, `appointed by the Minister this year` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Auditor-General was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN, `a public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may audit the Fund` IF
        `is the Auditor-General`
    OR  (`appointed by the Minister this year` AND `the Auditor-General was consulted` AND `a public accountant`)

§§ `12 -- failing to give the auditor information`

-- s 12(1): the auditor or an authorised person "may require any person to furnish ... such information in the possession of that
-- person ... or to which that person ... has access as the auditor considers necessary". (2): "Any person who, without reasonable
-- excuse, fails to comply with any requirement of the auditor under subsection (1) or who otherwise hinders, obstructs or delays the
-- auditor" is guilty of an offence, "liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000". No imprisonment.
-- READING (an inference): "without reasonable excuse" is read as qualifying only the failure to comply, where the words stand.
GIVEN `required by the auditor to give information` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the auditor offence` IF
        (`required by the auditor to give information` AND (NOT `complied`) AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`))
    OR  `hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor`

§§ `14 -- false statements and documents`

-- s 14: "Any person who for any purpose connected with this Act -- (a) knowingly makes any false statement to the Minister or a person
-- authorised by the Minister or to the auditor or a person authorised by the auditor; or (b) produces or furnishes or causes or
-- knowingly allows to be produced or furnished to [the same people] any document which the person knows to be false in a material
-- particular" -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000". No imprisonment.
-- A training provider or employer running a scheme is a listed recipient only if authorised by the Minister; the Act does not say
-- who is. An unauthorised one is modelled as outside s 14.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the Minister`
    `a person authorised by the Minister`
    `the auditor`
    `a person authorised by the auditor`
    `a training provider not authorised by the Minister`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a listed recipient` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a training provider not authorised by the Minister` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `for a purpose connected with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `made a false statement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew the statement was false` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave a document false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew the document was false` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the false information offence` IF
        `for a purpose connected with the Act`
    AND `is a listed recipient` `the recipient`
    AND (    (`made a false statement` AND `knew the statement was false`)
         OR  (`gave a document false in a material particular` AND `knew the document was false`))

§§ `12, 14 -- maximum penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to assist the auditor`
    `giving false information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to assist the auditor` THEN 1000
    WHEN `giving false information` THEN 5000

§§ `15 -- directors, partners and officers`

-- s 15(1): where an offence "has been committed by a body corporate, a partnership, or an unincorporated association of persons, any
-- person who, at the time of the commission of the offence, was a director, manager, partner, secretary or other similar officer
-- thereof, or was purporting to act in any such capacity, shall also be guilty of that offence ... unless the person proves that --
-- (a) the offence was committed without the person's consent or connivance; and (b) the person had exercised all such diligence to
-- prevent the commission of the offence as the person ought to have exercised". (2): where a body corporate's affairs are managed
-- by its members, "director" means a member.
-- The officer is guilty by default; to escape, the officer must prove BOTH limbs. Proving only no consent is not enough.
GIVEN `the organisation committed an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `held or purported to hold such an office at the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the organisation committed an offence under the Act`
    AND `held or purported to hold such an office at the time`
    AND (NOT (`proved no consent or connivance` AND `proved all due diligence`))

§§ `16 -- composition`

-- s 16(1): the Minister or an authorised person "may compound any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a compoundable
-- offence by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum of money not exceeding $500".
-- (2): "On payment of the sum of money, no further proceedings are to be taken against that person in respect of the offence."
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `the sum` AT MOST 500

GIVEN `compounded` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `further proceedings are barred` IF
    `compounded` AND `the sum was paid`

§§ `Schedule paras 1(3), 3, 6 -- the Advisory Council`

-- Para 1(3): if the Minister is satisfied that a member "(a) is guilty of neglect of duty or misconduct; (b) has become bankrupt or
-- made an arrangement with his or her creditors; (c) is incapacitated by physical or mental illness; or (d) is otherwise unable or
-- unfit to discharge the functions of a member, the Minister may remove the member from office."
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `neglect of duty or misconduct`
    `bankruptcy or an arrangement with creditors`
    `incapacity through physical or mental illness`
    `otherwise unable or unfit`
    `disagreeing with the Minister`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `the Minister is satisfied of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may remove the member` IF
        `the Minister is satisfied of it`
    AND CONSIDER `the ground`
        WHEN `disagreeing with the Minister` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Para 3: "At any meeting of the Council, one-half of the number of members constitutes a quorum." Read as: present at least half
-- of the members (for an odd number, half rounded up, since a fraction of a member cannot attend -- an inference).
GIVEN `members` IS A NUMBER, `present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `present` TIMES 2 AT LEAST `members`

-- Para 6: questions are "decided by a majority of votes of the members present and, in the case of an equality of votes, the
-- chairperson or member presiding has a casting vote."
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `casting vote for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the motion carries` IF
        `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `casting vote for`)
